{
  "$comment": "The M4 Part B card schema, as data. Two things read this file and nothing else defines the decks: scripts/validate-decks.mjs (Node, zero deps) and src/game/voice/cards.ts (the engine's loader). A writer tuning a deck changes the JSON here and both sides follow. 'required' tags must be present and in 'values'; optional tags may be absent, and 'default' says what the engine assumes when they are. 'coverage' lists the tag tuples the validator reports zero-card gaps for. 'alias' maps a legacy tag name onto its modern one, so the M3 files still validate.",
  "burnTiers": {
    "run-to-run": "Never repeated across runs: burned in localStorage until the deck is exhausted, then reshuffled.",
    "within-run": "Never repeated within one run.",
    "free": "May repeat."
  },
  "common": {
    "slots": ["detective", "name", "place", "object", "time"],
    "statuses": ["generated", "kept", "tuned", "cut", "placeholder"],
    "optionalTags": {
      "mood": { "values": ["flat", "wry", "menace", "grief", "tired", "tender"] },
      "intensity": { "values": [1, 2, 3] }
    }
  },
  "$commonFieldsNote": "M4b §A.2 and §A.5. Two fields every card in every deck may carry, written TOP-LEVEL — siblings of `tags`, not inside it. `motifs` is a list and `tags` is for the single values the dealer matches on; `weather` excludes a card from the night outright rather than ranking it, which is not what a tag does either. The engine also reads `tags.motifs` and `tags.weather`, so a deck written the other way still scores, and arrivals keeps its M4 `tags.weather` where its own spec requires it.",
  "commonFields": {
    "motifs": {
      "list": true,
      "vocab": "motifs",
      "max": 3,
      "$note": "One to three words from content/motifs.json and nowhere else. The validator rejects anything outside that vocabulary and reports per-deck coverage. Zero is allowed on a card with no image in it."
    },
    "weather": {
      "default": "any",
      "vocab": "weather",
      "extraValues": ["any"],
      "$note": "The sky the card implies, including by its clothing — a raincoat, a collar turned up, wet boots. A card that names another sky than the night's never appears in that run."
    }
  },
  "$commonTagsNote": "M4b §A.3. One tag every deck may carry, merged underneath each deck's own, so a deck that already declares it — portraits.gender is required, business.gender has been optional since M4 — keeps its own stricter spec. It marks a card with a gendered pronoun in it; the engine filters on the subject's gender for similes about a body or a voice, and for business.",
  "commonTags": {
    "gender": { "required": false, "default": "any", "values": ["m", "f", "any"] }
  },
  "$vocabFilesNote": "A vocabulary too long to keep in two places lives in its own file, and both readers — scripts/validate-decks.mjs and src/game/voice/cards.ts — resolve it from there. The motif vocabulary is the only one so far: 70 words in seven groups, and duplicating it here is how it would drift.",
  "vocabFiles": { "motifs": "motifs.json" },
  "vocab": {
    "mood": ["flat", "wry", "menace", "grief", "tired", "tender"],
    "fixtureRole": [
      "bartender",
      "doorman",
      "newsstand",
      "counterman",
      "ticket-taker",
      "elevator-man",
      "landlady",
      "beat-cop",
      "cabbie",
      "druggist"
    ],
    "temper": ["enigma", "plain", "yap"],
    "register": ["truth", "evasion", "lie"],
    "placeKind": ["private", "semi", "public"],
    "hourBand": ["midnight-2", "2-4", "4-6", "6-8"],
    "weather": ["clear", "rain", "fog", "cold"],
    "circumstance": [
      "behind-on-rent",
      "flush",
      "hungover",
      "bruised",
      "off-a-divorce-case",
      "sleepless",
      "just-paid"
    ],
    "relationship": ["none", "someone-waiting", "someone-who-left", "complicated"],
    "caseState": ["cold", "warm", "hot", "tight"],
    "suspectClass": ["money", "working", "underworld", "professional", "any"],
    "factKind": [
      "personAt",
      "personNotAt",
      "denial",
      "objectMissing",
      "noiseAt",
      "timeOfDeath",
      "hasMotive",
      "hadAccess",
      "victimAliveAt",
      "victimDeadBy",
      "methodEvidence",
      "secretExplained"
    ],
    "anchorTemplate": [
      "bar-radio",
      "regular-stool",
      "cop-pass",
      "piano-lesson",
      "el-train",
      "church-bells",
      "last-edition",
      "fuse",
      "rain",
      "milk-wagon",
      "theater-out",
      "garage-shift",
      "drunk-singing",
      "dumbwaiter",
      "ice-delivery",
      "steam-whistle"
    ]
  },
  "decks": {
    "similes": {
      "file": "similes.json",
      "deckValues": ["similes", "simile"],
      "idPrefix": "SIM",
      "placeholderPrefix": "sim-p",
      "burn": "run-to-run",
      "target": 300,
      "slots": ["detective", "name", "place", "object", "time"],
      "tags": {
        "mood": { "required": true, "vocab": "mood" },
        "target": {
          "required": true,
          "values": [
            "face",
            "hands",
            "voice",
            "room",
            "street",
            "weather",
            "money",
            "lie",
            "silence",
            "drink",
            "body",
            "clothes",
            "city"
          ]
        },
        "intensity": { "required": true, "values": [1, 2, 3] }
      },
      "coverage": [["target", "intensity"]]
    },
    "portraits": {
      "file": "portraits.json",
      "deckValues": ["portraits", "portrait"],
      "idPrefix": "POR",
      "placeholderPrefix": "por-p",
      "burn": "run-to-run",
      "target": 150,
      "slots": ["detective", "name"],
      "tags": {
        "component": { "required": true, "values": ["trait", "habit", "clothing"] },
        "gender": { "required": true, "values": ["m", "f", "any"] },
        "class": { "required": true, "vocab": "suspectClass" },
        "ageBand": { "required": false, "default": "middle", "values": ["young", "middle", "old", "any"] }
      },
      "coverage": [["component", "gender"], ["component", "class"]]
    },
    "business": {
      "file": "business.json",
      "deckValues": ["business"],
      "idPrefix": "BUS",
      "placeholderPrefix": "bus-p",
      "burn": "free",
      "target": 120,
      "slots": ["detective", "name", "place", "object", "time"],
      "$genderNote": "A business card that says 'he' or 'she' belongs to a person of that gender and to nobody else — 'folded the newspaper she'd been reading' on a man is the tell. Tag every card that carries a gendered pronoun; a card with no pronoun in it is 'any' and goes to anybody. The engine treats this as a filter and not as a preference: it would rather deal a card of the wrong temper than one that calls a woman 'he'.",
      "tags": {
        "role": { "required": true, "vocab": "fixtureRole", "extraValues": ["suspect", "any"] },
        "temper": { "required": true, "vocab": "temper", "extraValues": ["any"] },
        "gender": { "required": false, "default": "any", "values": ["m", "f", "any"] }
      },
      "coverage": [["role", "temper"]]
    },
    "dashiell-lines": {
      "file": "dashiell.json",
      "deckValues": ["dashiell-lines", "dashiell"],
      "idPrefix": "HUM",
      "placeholderPrefix": "hum-p",
      "burn": "free",
      "target": 80,
      "$slotNote": "{name} is the SUBJECT of the question — whoever or whatever Dashiell is asking about — and never the person he is asking. The two coincide for exactly two kinds: 'ask-evening' and 'ask-hired' are questions about the person in front of him, so there {name} is the addressee. Everywhere else, use {addressee} for a vocative ('The {object}, {addressee}.') and {name} only for the subject ('Tell me about {name}.'). {place} and {object} are the place or thing the question is about, not the room the page happens in. A card with {name} is dealt only when the topic names a person; a topic that names none — an anchor, a noise — is asked for with {topic}.",
      "slots": ["detective", "name", "addressee", "place", "object", "time", "topic"],
      "tags": {
        "kind": {
          "required": true,
          "values": [
            "open",
            "ask-person",
            "ask-place",
            "ask-object",
            "ask-evening",
            "ask-hired",
            "follow-up",
            "close"
          ]
        },
        "familiar": { "required": true, "values": ["yes", "no"] }
      },
      "coverage": [["kind", "familiar"]]
    },
    "frames": {
      "file": "frames.json",
      "deckValues": ["frames", "frame"],
      "idPrefix": "FRM",
      "placeholderPrefix": "frm-p",
      "burn": "within-run",
      "target": 110,
      "minPerCoverageCell": 4,
      "slots": ["detective", "name", "place", "object", "time", "fact", "business", "colour", "dashiell"],
      "requiredSlots": ["fact"],
      "tags": {
        "register": { "required": true, "vocab": "register" },
        "temper": { "required": true, "vocab": "temper" },
        "familiar": { "required": true, "values": ["yes", "no"] }
      },
      "coverage": [["register", "temper", "familiar"]]
    },
    "utterances": {
      "file": "utterances.json",
      "deckValues": ["utterances", "utterance"],
      "idPrefix": "UTT",
      "placeholderPrefix": "utt-p",
      "burn": "free",
      "target": 160,
      "minPerCoverageCell": 3,
      "$comment": "The engine adds four slots to Part B's four, because four fact kinds carry something none of {subject}/{place}/{time}/{object} can hold: {window} (the coroner's span), {motive}, {method} and {secret}. An utterance that does not carry its fact kind's mandatory slots (see mandatorySlots) does not fit, and the engine falls back to the clue's flat text in quotation marks and logs the gap.",
      "slots": [
        "detective",
        "name",
        "subject",
        "place",
        "object",
        "time",
        "window",
        "motive",
        "method",
        "secret"
      ],
      "mandatorySlots": {
        "personAt": ["subject", "place", "time"],
        "personNotAt": ["subject", "place", "time"],
        "denial": ["subject", "time"],
        "objectMissing": ["object"],
        "noiseAt": ["place", "time"],
        "timeOfDeath": ["window"],
        "hasMotive": ["subject", "motive"],
        "hadAccess": ["subject", "place"],
        "victimAliveAt": ["time"],
        "victimDeadBy": ["time"],
        "methodEvidence": ["method"],
        "secretExplained": ["subject", "secret"]
      },
      "tags": {
        "factKind": { "required": true, "vocab": "factKind" },
        "temper": { "required": true, "vocab": "temper" },
        "register": { "required": false, "default": "truth", "vocab": "register", "extraValues": ["any"] }
      },
      "coverage": [["factKind", "temper"]]
    },
    "find": {
      "file": "find.json",
      "deckValues": ["find"],
      "idPrefix": "FND",
      "placeholderPrefix": "fnd-p",
      "burn": "within-run",
      "target": 50,
      "slots": ["detective", "name", "place", "object", "time", "fact"],
      "warnSlots": {
        "fact": "the clue's own record has nowhere to land inside the card, so the engine appends it as a second sentence instead of the writer choosing where it falls"
      },
      "tags": {
        "clueKind": { "required": true, "values": ["physical", "document", "morgue", "scene"] },
        "placeKind": { "required": false, "default": "any", "vocab": "placeKind", "extraValues": ["any"] }
      },
      "coverage": [["clueKind", "placeKind"]]
    },
    "arrivals": {
      "file": "arrivals.json",
      "deckValues": ["arrivals", "arrival"],
      "idPrefix": "ARR",
      "placeholderPrefix": "arr-p",
      "burn": "within-run",
      "target": 60,
      "slots": ["detective", "name", "place", "object", "time"],
      "tags": {
        "placeKind": { "required": true, "vocab": "placeKind", "extraValues": ["any"] },
        "hourBand": { "required": true, "vocab": "hourBand", "extraValues": ["any"] },
        "weather": { "required": true, "vocab": "weather", "extraValues": ["any"] }
      },
      "coverage": [["placeKind", "hourBand"], ["placeKind", "weather"]]
    },
    "transitions": {
      "file": "transitions.json",
      "deckValues": ["transitions", "transition"],
      "idPrefix": "TRN",
      "placeholderPrefix": "trn-p",
      "burn": "free",
      "target": 80,
      "slots": ["detective", "name", "place", "object", "time"],
      "tags": {
        "hourBand": { "required": true, "vocab": "hourBand", "extraValues": ["any"] },
        "anchorTemplate": { "required": false, "vocab": "anchorTemplate" }
      },
      "coverage": [["hourBand"], ["anchorTemplate"]]
    },
    "ambient": {
      "file": "ambient.json",
      "deckValues": ["ambient"],
      "idPrefix": "AMB",
      "placeholderPrefix": "amb-p",
      "burn": "within-run",
      "target": 120,
      "slots": ["detective", "name", "place", "object", "time"],
      "tags": {
        "hourBand": { "required": true, "vocab": "hourBand", "extraValues": ["any"] },
        "caseState": { "required": true, "vocab": "caseState", "extraValues": ["any"] },
        "circumstance": { "required": false, "default": "any", "vocab": "circumstance", "extraValues": ["any"] }
      },
      "coverage": [["hourBand", "caseState"]]
    },
    "asides": {
      "file": "asides.json",
      "deckValues": ["asides", "aside"],
      "idPrefix": "ASD",
      "placeholderPrefix": "asd-p",
      "burn": "run-to-run",
      "target": 60,
      "slots": ["detective", "name", "place", "time"],
      "tags": {
        "relationship": { "required": true, "vocab": "relationship", "extraValues": ["any"] },
        "circumstance": { "required": true, "vocab": "circumstance", "extraValues": ["any"] }
      },
      "coverage": [["relationship", "circumstance"]]
    },
    "places": {
      "file": "places.json",
      "deckValues": ["places", "place"],
      "idPrefix": "PLACE",
      "placeholderPrefix": "plc-p",
      "burn": "within-run",
      "target": 110,
      "slots": ["detective", "name", "place", "object", "time"],
      "tags": {
        "placeKind": { "required": true, "vocab": "placeKind" },
        "watcher": {
          "required": false,
          "default": "none",
          "alias": "fixtureRole",
          "vocab": "fixtureRole",
          "extraValues": ["none"]
        },
        "empty": { "required": false, "default": "no", "values": ["yes", "no"] }
      },
      "coverage": [["placeKind", "watcher"], ["placeKind", "empty"]]
    },
    "endings": {
      "file": "endings.json",
      "deckValues": ["endings", "ending"],
      "idPrefix": "END",
      "placeholderPrefix": "end-p",
      "$burnNote": "A.8 names similes, portraits and asides as the run-to-run decks and does not name this one. The closing page is scored by a pure function that is recomputed on every render, so it has nowhere to write a burn; the card is drawn off the case seed instead, which keeps one case's ending the same however many times it is looked at.",
      "burn": "free",
      "target": 24,
      "slots": ["detective", "name", "place", "object", "time", "missed", "killer"],
      "tags": {
        "outcome": { "required": true, "values": ["hanged", "wrong-man", "thin-case", "cold"] },
        "parDelta": { "required": true, "values": ["under", "at", "over"] }
      },
      "coverage": [["outcome", "parDelta"]]
    },
    "office": {
      "optional": true,
      "file": "office.json",
      "deckValues": ["office"],
      "idPrefix": "OFF",
      "placeholderPrefix": "off-p",
      "burn": "within-run",
      "target": 30,
      "$comment": "M4b §B.2.1. Two rooms over a tailor's, at midnight, before anybody has knocked. This is the one deck where Dashiell's circumstance is allowed to be plot: behind on rent means the envelope is on the desk and the retainer matters. One card is the first paragraph of every run, so the deck is small and every card in it has to be able to open a book.",
      "slots": ["detective", "name", "place", "object", "time"],
      "tags": {
        "circumstance": { "required": true, "vocab": "circumstance", "extraValues": ["any"] },
        "weather": { "required": false, "default": "any", "vocab": "weather", "extraValues": ["any"] }
      },
      "coverage": [["circumstance"], ["circumstance", "weather"]]
    },
    "entrances": {
      "optional": true,
      "file": "entrances.json",
      "deckValues": ["entrances", "entrance"],
      "idPrefix": "ENT",
      "placeholderPrefix": "ent-p",
      "burn": "within-run",
      "target": 40,
      "$comment": "M4b §B.2.2. How the client comes through the door. The engine weaves the client's portrait into this per §A.4, so a card should leave room for a person rather than describe one: what the door did, what they did with their hat, how long they stood there. `familiar: yes` is for a client Dashiell already knows — the roll says so — and the card may say as much.",
      "slots": ["detective", "name", "place", "object", "time"],
      "tags": {
        "temper": { "required": true, "vocab": "temper", "extraValues": ["any"] },
        "class": { "required": true, "vocab": "suspectClass" },
        "gender": { "required": false, "default": "any", "values": ["m", "f", "any"] },
        "familiar": { "required": false, "default": "no", "values": ["yes", "no", "any"] },
        "weather": { "required": false, "default": "any", "vocab": "weather", "extraValues": ["any"] }
      },
      "coverage": [["temper", "class"], ["class", "gender"]]
    },
    "hiring": {
      "optional": true,
      "file": "hiring.json",
      "deckValues": ["hiring"],
      "idPrefix": "HIR",
      "placeholderPrefix": "hir-p",
      "burn": "within-run",
      "target": 20,
      "$comment": "M4b §B.2.3. The exchange that hires him, as one frame. `{fact}` is the client's own clue — why Dashiell was hired — and `{retainer}` is what the money looks like on the desk, by the client's class: twenty dollars from a working man, fifty from a professional, a hundred from money, and a roll with a rubber band round it from the underworld. The engine fills `{retainer}`; a card that leaves it out gets no money in it, and this is the one page where the money is the point.",
      "slots": ["detective", "name", "place", "object", "time", "fact", "retainer", "business", "colour", "dashiell"],
      "requiredSlots": ["fact"],
      "warnSlots": {
        "retainer": "the page never says what the job pays, and §B.2 asks that the player always knows they are being paid"
      },
      "tags": {
        "temper": { "required": true, "vocab": "temper", "extraValues": ["any"] },
        "familiar": { "required": false, "default": "no", "values": ["yes", "no", "any"] }
      },
      "coverage": [["temper", "familiar"]]
    },
    "witness": {
      "file": "witness.json",
      "deckValues": ["witness"],
      "idPrefix": "WIT",
      "placeholderPrefix": "wit-p",
      "burn": "within-run",
      "target": 50,
      "legacy": "M3's one-card-per-answer deck. The M4 exchange is built from frames × dashiell-lines × utterances instead, so nothing deals this any more. Kept so the file still validates and so a writer can mine it.",
      "slots": ["detective", "name", "place", "object", "time"],
      "tags": {
        "fixtureRole": { "required": true, "vocab": "fixtureRole", "extraValues": ["secretary", "neighbor", "business-partner", "relative"] },
        "register": { "required": true, "vocab": "register" }
      },
      "coverage": [["fixtureRole", "register"]]
    }
  }
}
